# Development environment. Copy to .env.local.
#
# Bootstrap a new checkout once with `npx convex dev --configure`, which
# creates the deployment and writes CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT for you. Task worktrees
# read this file from the primary checkout, so it is written once per machine.
# Vite dev and preview both serve http://localhost:8050 and stop if it is busy.

CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=
VITE_CONVEX_URL=
VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL=

# Frontend deployment identity. Local development defaults to this US-only
# topology when these values are omitted. Production builds require them.
VITE_JORI_REGION=us
VITE_JORI_ENABLED_REGIONS=us
VITE_JORI_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8050
VITE_JORI_US_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8050
# VITE_JORI_EU_ORIGIN=https://eu.example.com

# Analytics stays disabled in development. When enabled, every enabled
# region needs its public PostHog project token.
# VITE_POSTHOG_ENABLED=false
# VITE_POSTHOG_US_KEY=

# Sandbox credentials belong on the selected Convex deployment.

# Convex deployment envs, not Vite envs. Set them on the deployment with:
#
#   npx convex env set JORI_APP_URL "http://localhost:8050"
#   npx convex env set JORI_REGION "us"
#   npx convex env set JORI_PUBLIC_ORIGIN "http://localhost:8050"
#
# Better Auth runs inside the Convex deployment and needs its own deployment
# envs: BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET,
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID, MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET, and
# JORI_APP_URL as the app origin. Sign-in resolves every social credential on
# each request, so a missing Microsoft secret breaks Google sign-in too.
# Register development social sign-in redirect URIs on the provider apps:
#   http://localhost:8050/api/auth/callback/google
#   http://localhost:8050/api/auth/callback/microsoft
# Connector OAuth callbacks remain on the Convex site URL.
#
# Jori sends from one hardcoded address on mail.usejori.com, so this
# deployment's BIRD_API_KEY must have sending access to that domain and match
# JORI_REGION. Set BIRD_WORKSPACE_ID to the same key's workspace. Development
# uses its own key, never a production key. No email webhook is required.
#
# Agent runs execute inside the Convex deployment, so their credentials are
# deployment envs too: OPENROUTER_API_KEY to deduce, and BL_API_KEY, BL_WORKSPACE,
# JORI_BLAXEL_IMAGE and DO_NOT_TRACK=1 to open a sandbox.
# Web search and website discovery require PARALLEL_API_KEY. Configure
# PARALLEL_SEARCH_BASE_URL and PARALLEL_EXTRACT_BASE_URL on each deployment.
# Both use https://api.parallel.ai in dev. EU production uses a separate Search origin.
# Billing requires STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET, and
# STRIPE_PRICE_{STARTER,TEAM}_{MONTH,YEAR}.
#
# NOTION_WEBHOOK_VERIFICATION_TOKEN is required for signed Notion webhook
# deliveries after subscription verification.
# Use separate development registrations for GitHub, Slack, Linear and Notion.
# Their OAuth, signing and app credentials belong in this Convex deployment.
# Follow docs/integrations.md for regional registration and branding guidance.
